@startuml architecture_layers

skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor White
skinparam rectangleBorderColor Black
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

title Three-Layer Architecture: Calculator Application

rectangle "ORCHESTRATION LAYER" #FFE5E5 {
    rectangle CLI [
        <b>CLI Interface</b>
        ----
        CalculatorCLI
        ----
        <i>Coordinates user input with services
        Manages interactive and CLI modes</i>
    ]

    rectangle GUI [
        <b>GUI Interface</b>
        ----
        CalculatorGUI
        ----
        <i>Tkinter-based graphical interface
        Delegates calculations to service</i>
    ]

    rectangle EntryPoint [
        <b>Entry Point</b>
        ----
        __main__.py
        ----
        <i>Dispatches to CLI or GUI mode</i>
    ]
}

rectangle "CALCULATION ENGINE LAYER" #DDFFD4 {
    rectangle CalcEngine [
        <b>Core Computation</b>
        ----
        CalculationEngine (Protocol)
        Calculator (basic ops)
        ScientificCalculator (extended ops)
        ----
        <i>Pluggable calculation implementations
        No dependencies on storage or history</i>
    ]

    rectangle CalcService [
        <b>Calculation Service</b>
        ----
        CalculatorService
        ----
        <i>Composes calculator + storage
        Executes operations, tracks timing</i>
    ]
}

rectangle "HISTORY & STORAGE LAYER" #FFF3CC {
    rectangle StorageComp [
        <b>Storage Backend</b>
        ----
        StorageBackend (Protocol)
        JsonStorage
        ----
        <i>Persists CalculationResult
        File I/O implementation</i>
    ]

    rectangle HistoryComp [
        <b>History Services</b>
        ----
        MemoryBackend (Protocol)
        MemoryService
        StatisticsService
        ImportExportService
        ----
        <i>In-memory history management
        Analytics and import/export</i>
    ]
}

EntryPoint --> CLI : dispatches to
EntryPoint --> GUI : dispatches to
CLI --> CalcService : uses
GUI --> CalcService : uses
CalcService --> CalcEngine : depends on\n(CalculationEngine)
CalcService --> StorageComp : depends on\n(StorageBackend)
HistoryComp --> StorageComp : may persist\nto
CLI -.-> HistoryComp : optional\nuse

note bottom of CalcEngine
  Dependencies are protocol-based (interfaces)
  Concrete implementations (Calculator, ScientificCalculator)
  are swappable at runtime
end note

note bottom of StorageComp
  StorageBackend protocol decouples
  CalculatorService from storage details
  JsonStorage is current implementation
end note

note bottom of HistoryComp
  MemoryBackend protocol decouples
  Statistics and ImportExport from
  MemoryService internals
end note

@enduml
